The Prosperity Passport is a Web3 identity solution powered by non-transferable Soulbound Tokens (SBTs), first proposed by Ethereum co-founder Vitalik Buterin. Unlike traditional NFTs, SBTs are permanently tied to a single blockchain address, making them ideal for representing unique, verifiable attributes such as identity, reputation, or achievements. Launched on March 10, 2023, by Masa and the Celo Foundation, the Prosperity Passport enables over 10 million unique Celo wallet holders to mint a digital identity and claim a .celo domain name, similar to Ethereum’s ENS domains.

The Prosperity Passport serves as a gateway to on-chain tools and real-world utilities within the Celo ecosystem. It allows users to verify their identity through simple processes like CAPTCHA and two-factor authentication, minting a Masa Green SBT to confirm they are not bots. This verified status unlocks access to a range of benefits, including micro-loans, universal basic income (UBI) programs, reputation scores, and other decentralized finance (DeFi) and decentralized application (dApp) functionalities.

Since its launch, the Prosperity Passport has seen remarkable adoption, with over 42,000 unique users minting SBTs and more than 258,000 .celo domain names claimed within the first 20 days. This rapid growth underscores its potential to transform how users interact with Web3 services on Celo.

